+# CONTRACT — Real-Time Collaborative Document Editor
+
+## Operational Transform core (`src/ot.ts`)
+- [ ] `apply(content, op)` applies an insert op → test: insert "X" at pos returns new string
+- [ ] `apply(content, op)` applies a delete op → test: delete removes the right slice
+- [ ] `apply` rejects out-of-bounds ops → test: throws on invalid pos/length
+- [ ] `transform(a, b)` insert/insert at different positions preserves both → test: convergence apply(apply(c,a),b') == apply(apply(c,b),a')
+- [ ] `transform` insert/insert at same position preserves BOTH (no drop) → test: both texts present, deterministic order via tie-break
+- [ ] `transform` insert/delete and delete/insert converge → test: convergence property
+- [ ] `transform` delete/insert where insert lands inside deleted range preserves the insert → test: inserted text survives
+- [ ] `transform` delete/delete overlapping converges, no double-delete → test: convergence property
+- [ ] Randomized convergence: for many random op pairs on random strings, both transform orders converge → test: property test over 500 cases
+
+## REST API (`src/server.ts`)
+- [ ] POST /api/documents creates doc → 201 with {id,title,content,version}
+- [ ] POST with missing title → 400
+- [ ] GET /api/documents lists docs → 200 array
+- [ ] GET /api/documents/:id returns doc → 200; unknown id → 404
+- [ ] PUT /api/documents/:id updates title/content, bumps version → 200; unknown → 404
+- [ ] DELETE /api/documents/:id removes doc → 204; unknown → 404
+- [ ] GET /api/documents/:id/versions returns version history → 200 array ordered by version
+
+## WebSocket collaboration
+- [ ] Connect to /ws/documents/:id → receive sync message with current content+version
+- [ ] Connect to unknown doc id → error message + close
+- [ ] Send op → server applies, broadcasts transformed op+version to all clients
+- [ ] Two clients editing concurrently (different base versions) converge → test: both clients & REST agree
+- [ ] Malformed op (bad JSON / bad shape / out-of-bounds) → error message, server does NOT crash
+- [ ] 10 concurrent clients each sending ops → all converge to identical content, no corruption
+
+## Persistence
+- [ ] Documents + versions survive server restart → test: create+edit, stop, new createApp on same file, content+versions intact
+
+## Factory contract
+- [ ] `createApp(dbPath?)` returns `{app, start(port?), stop()}`
+- [ ] `start(0)` listens on random port and returns the actual port number
+- [ ] `stop()` closes HTTP server, all WS connections, and DB cleanly
+
+## Build / Lint
+- [ ] `npm run build` compiles with no errors
+- [ ] `npm run lint` passes
+- [ ] `npm run test` all green
